Quoting  sjdevnull@yahoo.com <sjdevnull@yahoo.com>:
>It's also important to realize that the benefit of AC isn't linear.
>Getting from 10 to 0 AC is _far_ more helpful than getting from 0 to
>-10 AC.  Indeed, getting from 10 to 0 AC is _far_ more helpful than
>getting from -10 to -50 AC.
>Points of AC down to AC 0 stop things from hitting you as often.
>Beyond that, they only decrease how much damage things do on average,

That is not true. Negative AC also decreases monsters' chance to hit by
counting as a random AC between -1 and the actual AC.

>but that decrease is random (from as little as 1hp off no matter how
>low your AC up to the max).  So every additional point of AC below 0 is
>worth less and less.

That's sort of true, but ignores the fact that while (say) reducing
incoming damage from 100% to 90% has eliminated only 10% of incoming
damage, reducing it from 20% to 10% has eliminated 50% of incoming damage
(before that last change) - ie, the reduction is less for each point below
0, but a reduction is worth more the more reduction you have already.

